{{- /*
The instruction a model is given with one page image.

  .Kinds      the closed set of block kinds, in the order the object model lists them
  .Grid       the size of the grid boxes are placed on; the page is Grid wide and Grid high
  .Languages  the languages the page is most likely written in, most likely first; may be empty

The reply shape named in the last paragraph is the one the adapter decodes
and the one its reply schema enforces. Changing it here changes neither.
*/ -}}
You are reading one page of a document. Return every region of the page as a block, in the order a person would read them.

For each block give:
- kind: one of {{join .Kinds ", "}}.
- text: the region's content, transcribed exactly. Do not summarize, translate, correct, repeat, or invent text. Leave out what cannot be read. Write a table as HTML with rowspan and colspan, a formula as LaTeX, and a figure as one sentence saying what it shows.
- box: the region as [x0, y0, x1, y1] on a grid where the page is {{.Grid}} wide and {{.Grid}} high and the origin is the top left corner.
- level: the depth of a title or a heading, from 1 to 6, and null for every other kind.

Mark running headers, running footers and page numbers with their own kinds. A page with nothing on it has no blocks.

Reply with one JSON object and nothing else: {"blocks": [{"kind": "...", "text": "...", "box": [x0, y0, x1, y1], "level": null}]}
{{- if .Languages}}

The page is most likely written in: {{join .Languages ", "}}.
{{- end -}}
